<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
	<Task>
		<Title>Rename Domain-Joined Windows Computer (SYSTEM + DomainCredential, Secure Parameters)</Title>
		<Description><![CDATA[
<P>Renames a domain-joined Windows computer <B>without creating a local logon token for the
supplied account at all</B>. The payload runs in the BigFix agent's own
<TT>NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM</TT> context - already fully elevated locally - and the domain account is
handed to <TT>Rename-Computer</TT> as <TT>-DomainCredential</TT>, i.e. used only as network
credentials for the Active Directory computer-object update.</P>

<P><B>Why this variant exists.</B> Every other elevation vehicle tried on this endpoint performs a
local logon for the domain account and fails before the rename is ever attempted: BigFix's own
<TT>override runas=localuser</TT> fails with RPC error 1783 (<TT>RPC_X_BAD_STUB_DATA</TT>),
<TT>Start-Process -Credential</TT> fails with "Access is denied" because a Session 0 service has no
interactive window station, and the Scheduled Task variant depends on a batch logon. This task
performs no local logon whatsoever, so none of those apply.</P>

<P><B>Requirements.</B> The supplied account needs rights on the target's AD computer object. Unlike
the <TT>Start-Process -Credential</TT> and Scheduled Task variants, it does <B>not</B> need to be a
local Administrator on the endpoint, and is not subject to any "Deny log on locally" / "Deny log on
as a batch job" policy, because it never logs on to the endpoint.</P>

<P><B>Credential handling.</B> The password is written by <TT>createfile</TT> (no shell involved, so
shell metacharacters in the password cannot be interpreted) into
<TT>%ProgramData%\BigFix\RenameComputer</TT>, which is ACL'd to SYSTEM and Administrators only. Only
the file <I>path</I> is passed on the command line. The script reads it into memory and deletes it in
a <TT>finally</TT> block; the action script deletes it again unconditionally as a safety net.</P>

<P><B>Scope warning.</B> Take this action against <B>one endpoint at a time</B>. The new name is a
single value, so targeting multiple computers would rename them all identically and cause a name
collision.</P>

<P><B>Result.</B> On success the computer is flagged as requiring a restart; the rename completes on
reboot. A log is left at <TT>&lt;BES Client&gt;\__BESData\__Global\Logs\rename-computer.log</TT>.</P>

<P>Supply the new computer name and the domain account's credentials below. The password field is
masked and delivered as a Secure Parameter - it is not shown in cleartext in this dialog, and is not
remembered as a default the way a plain action parameter would be.</P>

<P>
<LABEL for=newComputerName>New computer name (NetBIOS, max 15 characters): </LABEL><INPUT id=newComputerName name=newComputerName><BR>
<LABEL for=adminUser>Domain account (DOMAIN\user or user@domain.tld): </LABEL><INPUT id=adminUser name=adminUser><BR>
<LABEL for=adminPw>Account password: </LABEL><INPUT id=adminPw type=password name=adminPw><BR>
<LABEL for=adminPw2>Verify password: </LABEL><INPUT id=adminPw2 type=password name=adminPw2>
</P>
<script>
			document.body.ontakeaction = function() {
				var newComputerName = document.getElementById( "newComputerName" ).value;
				var adminUser = document.getElementById( "adminUser" ).value;
				var adminPw = document.getElementById( "adminPw" ).value;
				var adminPw2 = document.getElementById( "adminPw2" ).value;
				if (!newComputerName || newComputerName.length > 15 || !/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*$/.test(newComputerName) || /^[0-9]+$/.test(newComputerName)) {
					alert ("Please enter a valid NetBIOS computer name (max 15 characters, letters/digits/hyphen only, not all digits)."); return false; };
				if (!adminUser) {
					alert ("Please enter the domain account."); return false; };
				if (adminPw==null || adminPw=="") {
					alert ("The account's password is required."); return false; };
				if (adminPw !== adminPw2) {
					alert ("The passwords do not match."); return false; };
				else {TakeSecureFixletAction(Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), "Action1", {}, { newComputerName: newComputerName, adminUser: adminUser, adminPw: adminPw}); }
				return false; }
			</script> ]]></Description>
		<Relevance>windows of operating system</Relevance>
		<Relevance>version of client &gt;= "11.0.4"</Relevance>
		<Relevance>exists dns domainname of local computer of active directory</Relevance>
		<Relevance>exists value "PowerShellVersion" whose (it as string as version &gt;= "5.0") of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\PowerShell\3\PowerShellEngine" of native registry</Relevance>
		<Category>Configuration</Category>
		<Source>Internal</Source>
		<SourceID>Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential-SecureParam</SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-09-02</SourceReleaseDate>
		<SourceSeverity></SourceSeverity>
		<CVENames></CVENames>
		<SANSID></SANSID>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BESC</Domain>
		<DefaultAction ID="Action1">
			<Description>
				<PreLink>Click </PreLink>
				<Link>here</Link>
				<PostLink> to rename this computer.</PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[
// Renames the computer from the agent's own SYSTEM context, passing the domain account to
// Rename-Computer as -DomainCredential. There is no override runas=localuser, no
// Start-Process -Credential and no Scheduled Task here: nothing logs the account on to this
// endpoint, so none of the local-logon failures those vehicles hit can occur.
// See Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential.ps1.
// 2026-09-02 atlauren / Claude
//
// NOTE: relevance substitution runs over createfile bodies, so every literal { in the embedded
// PowerShell is doubled to {{. Closing } are left single - doubling them would emit literal }}
// into the deployed file and break it.

action uses wow64 redirection false

// newComputerName, adminUser and adminPw arrive as public/Secure Parameters supplied by the
// Description's custom HTML form and TakeSecureFixletAction, not via action parameter query -
// the native prompt dialog (and its unmasked password entry) is bypassed for this action.

// Validate before touching the endpoint.
continue if {(length of it >= 1 and length of it <= 15) of (parameter "newComputerName" of action)}
continue if {exists match (regex "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*$") of (parameter "newComputerName" of action)}
continue if {not exists match (regex "^[0-9]+$") of (parameter "newComputerName" of action)}
continue if {(parameter "adminUser" of action) != ""}
continue if {(parameter "adminPw" of action) != ""}

parameter "WorkDir" = "{(value of variable "ProgramData" of environment) & "\BigFix\RenameComputer"}"
folder create "{parameter "WorkDir"}"

// The payload runs as SYSTEM and briefly holds a credential file, so deny non-administrators
// the ability to read or tamper with either.
waithidden "{pathname of system folder}\icacls.exe" "{parameter "WorkDir"}" /inheritance:r /grant "*S-1-5-18:(OI)(CI)F" /grant "*S-1-5-32-544:(OI)(CI)F"

delete "{parameter "WorkDir"}\Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential.ps1"

createfile until _END_RENAME_SYSCRED_PS1_
#Requires -Version 5.0
[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
    [string] $NewName,

    [string] $AdminUser = '',

    # Path to a one-time file holding the domain account's password; read, then deleted.
    [string] $CredentialFile = '',

    [string] $ActionId = 'manual',

    [string] $LogPath = (Join-Path ([Environment]::GetFolderPath('ProgramFilesX86')) 'BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\__Global\Logs\rename-computer.log')
)

$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'

function Write-Log {{
    param([string] $Message)
    $line = (Get-Date).ToString('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss') + '  ' + $Message
    Write-Output $line
    Add-Content -LiteralPath $LogPath -Value $line -Encoding ASCII
}

function Get-AdminCredential {{
    param([string] $UserName, [string] $Path)
    if (-not $UserName -or -not $Path -or -not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path)) {{
        return $null
    }
    $secret = (Get-Content -LiteralPath $Path -Raw).TrimEnd("`r", "`n")
    if (-not $secret) {{
        return $null
    }
    $securePw = ConvertTo-SecureString -String $secret -AsPlainText -Force
    [PSCredential]::new($UserName, $securePw)
}

$cred = $null
try {{
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path (Split-Path -Parent $LogPath) -Force | Out-Null
    Write-Log ('--- BigFix action ' + $ActionId + ' started (SYSTEM + DomainCredential) ' + (Get-Date).ToString('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss zzz') + ' ---')
    Write-Log ('Rename requested: ' + $NewName)

    $me = [Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent()
    Write-Log ('Running as: ' + $me.Name)
    $isAdmin = [Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal]::new($me).IsInRole([Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]::Administrator)
    Write-Log ('Elevated: ' + $isAdmin)
    if (-not $isAdmin) {{
        Write-Log 'ERROR: not running with an Administrators token.'
        exit 12
    }

    if ($NewName.Length -gt 15 -or $NewName -notmatch '^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*$' -or $NewName -match '^[0-9]+$') {{
        Write-Log ('ERROR: invalid NetBIOS computer name: ' + $NewName)
        exit 10
    }

    if ($env:COMPUTERNAME -eq $NewName) {{
        Write-Log 'Computer already has the requested name. Nothing to do.'
        exit 0
    }

    $cred = Get-AdminCredential -UserName $AdminUser -Path $CredentialFile
    if (-not $cred) {{
        Write-Log 'ERROR: no domain credential available; SYSTEM authenticates to AD as COMPUTER$ and cannot rewrite its own object.'
        exit 14
    }
    Write-Log ('Domain credential built for: ' + $cred.UserName)

    # SYSTEM reads AD as COMPUTER$, which is enough for this lookup.
    $collision = $false
    try {{
        $searcher = [DirectoryServices.DirectorySearcher]::new()
        $searcher.Filter = '(&(objectCategory=computer)(cn=' + $NewName + '))'
        if ($null -ne $searcher.FindOne()) {{
            $collision = $true
        }
    }
    catch {{
        Write-Log ('WARNING: AD pre-flight check skipped: ' + $_.Exception.Message)
    }
    if ($collision) {{
        Write-Log ('ERROR: an AD computer object named ' + $NewName + ' already exists.')
        exit 11
    }

    Write-Log ('Renaming ' + $env:COMPUTERNAME + ' to ' + $NewName)
    $renamed = $false
    try {{
        Rename-Computer -NewName $NewName -DomainCredential $cred -Force -ErrorAction Stop
        $renamed = $true
        Write-Log 'Rename-Computer succeeded.'
    }
    catch {{
        Write-Log ('Rename-Computer failed: HResult=' + $_.Exception.HResult + ' ' + $_.Exception.Message)
        $cimArgs = @{{
            Name     = $NewName
            UserName = $cred.UserName
            Password = $cred.GetNetworkCredential().Password
        }
        $result = Invoke-CimMethod -ClassName Win32_ComputerSystem -MethodName Rename -Arguments $cimArgs
        $cimArgs = $null
        if ($result.ReturnValue -eq 0) {{
            $renamed = $true
            Write-Log 'Win32_ComputerSystem.Rename succeeded.'
        }
        else {{
            Write-Log ('Win32_ComputerSystem.Rename failed with return value ' + $result.ReturnValue)
        }
    }
    if (-not $renamed) {{
        exit 12
    }

    $staged = (Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\ComputerName\ComputerName' -Name 'ComputerName').ComputerName
    Write-Log ('Staged name in registry: ' + $staged)
    if ($staged -ne $NewName) {{
        Write-Log 'ERROR: post-rename verification failed.'
        exit 13
    }

    Write-Log 'Rename staged. Restart required to complete.'
    exit 0
}
catch {{
    Write-Log ('UNHANDLED ERROR: ' + $_.Exception.Message)
    exit 12
}
finally {{
    # Runs even on 'exit', so the secret never outlives the script regardless of which path ran.
    $cred = $null
    if ($CredentialFile) {{
        Remove-Item -LiteralPath $CredentialFile -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    }
}
_END_RENAME_SYSCRED_PS1_

move __createfile "{parameter "WorkDir"}\Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential.ps1"

// Written via createfile (not a shell command) so shell metacharacters in the password can't
// be interpreted; the file inherits the SYSTEM/Administrators-only ACL set above on WorkDir.
delete "{parameter "WorkDir"}\admin-syscred.cred"

createfile until _END_ADMIN_SYSCRED_CRED_
{parameter "adminPw" of action}
_END_ADMIN_SYSCRED_CRED_

move __createfile "{parameter "WorkDir"}\admin-syscred.cred"

// No override/runas, no seclogon dependency, no Scheduled Task: this runs as SYSTEM and the
// account is used only over the network, by Rename-Computer's -DomainCredential.
waithidden "{pathname of system folder}\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe" -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "{parameter "WorkDir"}\Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential.ps1" -NewName "{parameter "newComputerName" of action}" -AdminUser "{parameter "adminUser" of action}" -CredentialFile "{parameter "WorkDir"}\admin-syscred.cred" -ActionId "{id of action}" -LogPath "{storage folder of client}\__BESData\__Global\Logs\rename-computer.log"

// Capture the real result now, in case a later wait/waithidden ever overwrites "exit code of
// action". The delete commands below do not disturb it.
parameter "RenameResult" = "{exit code of action}"

// Safety net: the script already deletes the credential file in its finally block, but delete
// it again unconditionally in case the script died before reaching that point.
delete "{parameter "WorkDir"}\admin-syscred.cred"

continue if {(parameter "RenameResult" of action) = "0"}

delete "{parameter "WorkDir"}\Rename-DomainComputer-SystemCredential.ps1"

action requires restart "This computer was renamed. A restart is required to complete the change."
			]]></ActionScript>
			<SuccessCriteria Option="RunToCompletion"></SuccessCriteria>
		</DefaultAction>
	</Task>
</BES>
